// Complete project data guide, not a real project or a formal JSON configuration.
// Runtime skeleton: archifytemplate.json. Model authority: ../assets/model.js.
// Formal files are strict JSON with two-space indentation and a final newline.
// Generate new globally unique IDs; retain IDs when renaming. Remove example data.
// formatVersion is 1, independent of application version.
// repository.path is the code root; revision/dirty describe actual source state.
// Groups hold layers. A nonempty groupId must reference a real group.
// Group frames derive their bounds from members; x/y position an empty group.
// Module codeLocation is code-root-relative, newline-separated for multiple paths.
// appearance requires all three #rrggbb colors when supplied.
// status: planned=agreed design, verified=source evidence, modified=semantic edit.
// sources contain actually read repository-relative path, 1-based line, endLine, symbol.
// Verified items need at least one valid source. Never invent evidence.
// unknowns stays [] only after doubts are resolved. Templates are not project facts.
// requirements and dependencies are string arrays, one confirmed item per entry.
// Missing/empty defaultValue means no documented default; present values are strings.
// Structure fields have names, types and descriptions, without required/defaultValue.
// Methods remain in interfaces; flow/errors are newline-separated strings, not arrays.
// inputsConfirmed/outputsConfirmed must be true in a formal verified configuration.
// false plus an empty array does not establish absence; sample false values show a draft.
// Inputs require a boolean required flag; outputs use the same parameter model.
// Events use description, direction emit/receive, flow, parameters and reserved trigger.
// Tests describe steps/expected results, not evidence that a test actually passed.
// Relations connect two different module IDs. Ports: top/right/bottom/left.
// Optional legacy type is call/dependency; new arrows need no category.
// Relations annotate the canvas and do not substitute for explicit dependencies.
// view stores finite x/y, positive scale, and unique valid expanded item IDs.
